    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0961" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/204: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macgowan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-04T11:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 4—8:33
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Embassy informed. Spiridon Merculoff has resigned as President of the
                    Provisional Government. Successor is Yeremeiff, Mayor of Vladivostok.<anchor
                        n="70" xml:id="d734-f1"/> Immediate cause was the growing dissatisfaction
                        <pb facs="0962" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/> with the President’s dictatorial
                    ways though total bankruptcy of the Government and the retreat of the Army
                    contributed. Failure of the Army is due to lack of funds and ammunition and
                    excessive losses from frostbite.</p>
                <p>Situation unstable and there is talk about military dictatorship under General
                        Verschbitsky,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d734-f2"/> commanding the Army. Japanese
                    authorities watchful and doubtless they will shape the final result.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Macgowan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d734-f1" n="70" xml:id="d734-f1-content">
                <p>After a few days the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> under Merkulov was
                    restored.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d734-f2" n="71" xml:id="d734-f2-content">
                <p>Leader of the Kappel troops.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
